Experiment 44: To Automate File Upload Functionality on a Web Application Using Selenium WebDriver

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to automate file upload functionality on a web application.

## ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Launch the Chrome browser using Selenium WebDriver.
3. Open the file upload practice webpage.
4. Locate the file input element.
5. Specify the file path using `sendKeys()`.
6. Click the Upload button.
7. Verify the uploaded file name.
8. Close the browser.

## CODE

**File name: `FileUploadTest.java`**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.By;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class FileUploadTest {

    @Test
    public void uploadFile() {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/upload");

        driver.manage().window().maximize();

        WebElement uploadFile = driver.findElement(By.id("file-upload"));

        uploadFile.sendKeys("C:\\Users\\Public\\sample.txt");

        driver.findElement(By.id("file-submit")).click();

        String uploadedFile = driver.findElement(
            By.id("uploaded-files")
        ).getText();

        System.out.println("Uploaded File: " + uploadedFile);

        assertEquals("sample.txt", uploadedFile);

        System.out.println("File uploaded successfully.");

        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

## INPUT
- Website: https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/upload
- File name: `sample.txt`
- File path: `C:\Users\Public\sample.txt`

## EXPECTED OUTPUT

```text
Uploaded File: sample.txt
File uploaded successfully.
```

## RESULT
Thus, file upload functionality was automated successfully using Selenium WebDriver and the uploaded file was verified.
